        {
          "start": 12000,
          "end": 24000,
          "decision": "include",
          "reason": "The paper directly addresses what limits factual accuracy improvement in retrieval-augmented generation (RALM) by decomposing errors into Retriever Error, Hallucination Error, and Extraction Error, and showing that inconsistent error patterns across retrievers limit performance. It also proposes ensembling retrievers to improve accuracy.",
          "quoteId": "q51",
          "quoteHash": "a4a62eafb4565503edaa6ebe461cd4bcdd7ee1cd64c8115ace318a13334156b9"
        },
        {
          "start": 24000,
          "end": 36000,
          "decision": "include",
          "reason": "The paper directly addresses how retrieval-augmented generation can improve factual accuracy (via the EoR ensemble framework boosting RALM performance) and what limits that improvement, including incorrect retrieval, weak LM robustness to irrelevant/long context, distribution shift between train and test retriever performance, unpredictable reader model degeneration, and computational cost of ensembling multiple retrievers.",
          "quoteId": "q54",
          "quoteHash": "4cd5a41c9ac601547b1e910bc1b61951590db67fdc15ea3a78e7002e30b62c01"
